# The image is built from exactly two files — the Dockerfile COPYs
# entrypoint.sh and tools-smoke.sh and nothing else — so this is an allowlist
# rather than a list of things to leave out. A denylist has to be extended
# every time a file is added at the top level, and it was already stale:
# docker-compose.slim.sample.yml, .gitattributes and this file itself were all
# being uploaded as build context. Ignoring everything and re-including the two
# scripts keeps the context minimal by construction.
#
# Nothing here affects what ends up in the image (only a COPY can do that); it
# affects what is uploaded to the daemon, and it keeps a stray file — an
# operator's meshagent-data volume, an editor swap file, a .env — from being
# sent along with the build.
*
!entrypoint.sh
!tools-smoke.sh
